my name is Quintin Scranton I'm the  executive chef of crazy John's  restaurant in Lafayette Louisiana today  we're cooking crawfish croquettes  otherwise known as crawfish boudin balls  39 years ago prejean started as a  crawfish boiler room I would say pray  John's is legendary in Lafayette I  wanted to make a crawfish etouffee  boudin ball because it's my  grandmother's recipe so you're gonna  cook your vegetables first and then once  you add your tails you add the stock so  that they don't get rubbery and hard you  know I didn't think my grandmother  taught me much until I got older I  learned her little nuances and I learned  her attitude towards cooking her general  way that she feels about why she cooks I  wanted to make a crawfish boudin ball  out of her recipe to kind of make sure  that she sticks around  boudin traditionally from the French  style of cuisine but really it was made  in Louisiana rice is just as important  as protein and a poutine what I like to  do with these croquettes specifically is  add a little bit of Gouda cheese it  gives you a smoky flavor a little bit of  creaminess boon I got started because  people did not have enough meat they had  to use what they had which was starch or  rice they had to cut their sausage with  something a little bit more easily  accessible first it goes in the flour  then it goes into the egg wash and it  goes comes with a crack one batter then  it goes back into the egg wash then he  goes into the crack one batter for the  last time the cracklin batter is  something that gives you a little more  kick a little more Louisiana flavor then  we fry a pretty much made out of blue  there all right ate it since I was a  baby I can remember whenever I was six  years old at my uncle's restaurant he  just sat in the back and watched them  fry seafood and he's a prude and  sandwiches all day a lot of major  cultures they always congregate around  food crawfish etouffee is one of those  things for Cajun culture that people get  excited about the crawfish gives it  something that's more than a garnish  it's kind of something that it almost  sounded alone because it's such a pretty  presentation by itself when it comes to  what you see it's just as important to  what you taste eat with your eyes first  imagine salty spicy and crunchy on the  outside and then creamy me and filling  on the inside it's a delicious  bite-sized piece of heaven  [Music]  [Applause]
 

